# Files excluded from the Docker build context.
#
# The runtime stage of the Dockerfile copies only `dist/`, `node_modules/` and
# `package.json` from the builder, so source and tooling cannot reach the final
# image. This file matters for a second reason: everything not listed here is
# uploaded to the Docker daemon (and to a remote builder/CI) as build context,
# which slows builds and can leak local state.

# Dependencies (rebuilt inside the image for the correct platform)
node_modules/

# Build output (produced in the builder stage)
dist/
build/
*.tsbuildinfo

# Environment / secrets - never send these to a builder.
# The trailing negation keeps the committed template available if ever needed.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Version control
.git/
.gitignore
.gitattributes

# Host-run verification tooling (smoke tests, API correlation, scratch scripts).
# These run from the host against a published port and are not needed in the image.
scripts/

# Local log output
logs/
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
lerna-debug.log*

# Infrastructure / docs not needed to build the app
docker-compose*.yml
README.md
*.md

# IDE / editor state
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# AI agent + assistant state
.agents/
.copilot/
.github/
*.chatmode.md
*.instructions.md
*.prompt.md

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Testing / coverage output (tests run on the host, not in the image)
coverage/
.nyc_output/
*.lcov

# Temporary files
tmp/
temp/
*.tmp
*.temp
